   <text>
      <body>
         <div type="letter">
                <div type="address">
                    <ab> <address>
                            <addrLine>
                                <name type="geo" key="G_FRA_DIJO">Dijon</name>
                            </addrLine>
                        </address>
                    </ab>
                </div> <div type="mainBody">
                    <dateline>
                        <date when="1922-10-12">12/10/922</date>
                    </dateline>
                    <p>Dear Miss Weaver: I am <seg xml:id="seg1" type="note-anchor">on my way South</seg> with <rs type="person" key="barn84">my wife</rs> and <rs type="person" key="joyc07">daughter</rs> whom we could not leave alone in <name type="geo" key="G_FRA_PARI">Paris</name>. The <seg xml:id="seg2" type="note-anchor">second edition</seg> of <name type="work" key="W_ULYSSES">
                            <hi rend="underline">Ulysses</hi>
                        </name> was published this morning.</p>
                    <closer>
                        <salute>Kindest regards</salute>
                        <signed>
                            <name type="person" key="joyc82">James Joyce</name>
                        </signed>
                    </closer>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div type="notes">
                <note xml:id="note1" target="#seg1" type="commentary">On his way to Nice, JJ stopped in Dijon, where he met with printer <name type="person" key="dara82">Maurice Darantiere</name>.</note> <note xml:id="note2" target="#seg2" type="commentary">The plates of the first edition of <name type="work" key="W_ULYSSES">Ulysses</name> were also used for the second, “Published by the Egoist Press, London, by John Rodker, Paris.”</note>
            </div>
      </body>
